  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish several important ingredients but not their decisive combination. R7 demonstrates a highly accurate machine-learning interatomic potential for the closely related BCC MoNbTaW refractory HEA and examines SRO, while R8 identifies SRO and segregation thermodynamics in essentially the same W-Ta-Cr-V chemical system. R10 also shows the use and first-principles validation of empirical potentials for multicomponent HEAs. Other records connect finite-temperature electronic or magnetic free-energy terms to phase stability and show that SRO can alter physical properties. However, none describes training an MTP to reproduce the DFT liquid-phase distribution, replacing thermodynamic integration with MTP-to-DFT free-energy perturbation, exploiting the low variance of energy differences, or calculating melting-point shifts from electronic DOS and SRO contributions. Thus the literature points toward ML potentials and SRO-aware thermodynamics, but the specific MTP-plus-FEP melting workflow still requires a substantial new idea."
}
